  "alt": "Vector search in the browser spans three environments. The main thread spawns a Web Worker, the worker loads the WebAssembly engine into the WASM memory heap, where PGlite runs a full Postgres instance or SQLite-vec runs as an extension, and once the engine is ready the first vector query runs locally on the device.",
  "caption": "The main thread never blocks: the worker owns the engine, and every query stays on the device.",
